/-!
# Point deformation, invariant dimensions, and Young-subgroup configuration orbits

The point-set and invariant-dimension parts of the deformation argument are proved for
arbitrary finite families of distinct complex points, with arbitrary finite groups acting
by coordinate permutations. Polynomial interpolation identifies the coordinate algebra
with all functions on the point set. Its invariant algebra is the function algebra on
orbits. Averaging proves exactness on complex representations and additivity of fixed
space dimensions across every finite stable filtration.

`pointInitialIdeal` is the homogeneous ideal whose degree-n relations evaluate into the
strictly lower degree filtration. `pointInitialIdeal_eq_span_vanishing` proves that this
is exactly the ideal generated by top homogeneous parts of vanishing polynomials, using
bounds on degree that include the zero polynomial. No initial-ideal assertion is assumed.

`pointInitialQuotientGradedEquiv` identifies its quotient with the finite product of the
successive point-function degree layers. The equivalence is equivariant. Consequently:
* `pointInitialQuotient_finrank` proves finite-dimensionality and dimension equal to the
  number of distinct points.
* `pointInitialQuotient_fixed_finrank` proves invariant dimension equal to the number
  of point orbits. The proof uses exactness on the degree filtration, not a scalar bound.

These statements are instantiated on the `FullFlagStratumConfiguration` type,
including empty strata and zero-size alphabets. The site values are arbitrary distinct
complex numbers. `fullFlagStratumPoint_initial_fixed_finrank` gives the exact invariant
count for the initial algebra of each stratum point set. The Young subgroup is the actual
subgroup of position permutations preserving every colour class. Its orbits are exactly
site colour multisets, proved by constructing a permutation from equivalences of the
position fibers. `colourStratumPoint_initial_fixed_finrank` counts their attained values.
This last count is not identified here with the word catalog in the Levi assembly.

The elementary and root-power generators of the concrete full flag lie in this initial
ideal for every stratum: `fullFlagTruncationIdeal_le_pointInitialIdeal`. The elementary
values are constant because configurations with prescribed site multiplicities differ
by position permutations. The coordinate root powers are top components of products of
affine factors vanishing at all sites. The argument works uniformly in every parameter.

For the unrestricted configuration set this containment and the scalar upper
bound close the squeeze completely. `fullFlagTruncationIdeal_eq_pointInitialIdeal`
holds with no hypotheses beyond `2 * k <= B`. Thus `fullFlag_finrank_eq_configurations` gives
exact total dimension, and `fullFlag_invariant_finrank` gives the invariant dimension
of the actual `FullFlagRing B (B - k)` for every finite position group, including every
Young subgroup. Its orbit type uses threshold `k + 1` on the full alphabet, which imposes
no restriction; `fullFlagStratumConfiguration_allEquiv` identifies it with
all configurations.

Not proved here:
The refined stratum ring is not compared with its point initial algebra. The first
missing assertion, for distinct site values and admissible parameters, is

    remainderTopIdeal (fullFlagSubalphabet Y) (B - k) j <=
      pointInitialIdeal (fullFlagStratumPoint B k j Y zeta).

This requires both the vanishing of the deformed remainder minors on the selected
configuration stratum and identification of their highest homogeneous parts. Neither
assertion is supplied here. The all-row/top-row equality can be used in this step. Given
this containment, the proved elementary/root containment and
`fullFlagStratumIdeal_eq_pointInitialIdeal_of_le` give the refined equality of ideals.
The latter theorem is explicitly conditional on containment, not an unconditional result.

Further open items from the assembly audit:
* Identify the concrete Young-invariant full-flag quotient with `MixedRing q` modulo
  `middleFlagAllTailIdeal q (B - k)`, including contraction of the root-power ideal.
* Identify the attained site colour multisets with the retained word catalog, including
  stratum thresholds and multiplicities.
* Transport the strict graded minor certificate and refine the determinantal ideals
  into `MultiDoubledSiteCoefficientFlag`.
* Discharge the flags in `truncatedWeyl_sl4_multiDoubledSite_rank_le_of_flags`.
  `truncatedWeyl_sl4_multiDoubledSite_rank_le` is not proved or defined here.

Axiom check: all 97 explicit declarations (including 67 theorems) print
`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. No `sorry` is used.

Every explicit declaration is inventoried below, grouped by its source file. Each print
reports its actual dependencies.
-/

